---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
import RangeField from '../../components/RangeField.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Back-of-the-envelope numbers" hint="How much disk one server and one data center need when every server keeps a full copy, compared with a cache, and how many lookups still reach the storage servers. The sliders hold round numbers for practice, not Cloudflare's data.">
  <div class="pg est" data-est>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <RangeField label="Key-value pairs (billions)" name="k" min="1" max="10" step="1" value="5" />
      <RangeField label="Size of the whole dataset (TB)" name="s" min="0.5" max="4" step="0.1" value="1.6" />
      <RangeField label="Keys in use in this data center (%)" name="u" min="1" max="50" value="20" />
      <RangeField label="Servers in the data center" name="n" min="10" max="500" step="10" value="100" />
      <RangeField label="Storage servers that hold everything" name="w" min="2" max="8" value="3" />
      <RangeField label="Lookups per second in the data center (millions)" name="l" min="1" max="50" value="10" />
      <label>Hit rate of the data center's caches <select class="pg-in" data-h><option value="99">99%</option><option value="99.9">99.9%</option><option value="99.99" selected>99.99%</option><option value="99.999">99.999%</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <dl class="est-out" data-out aria-live="polite"></dl>
    <p class="pg-note">A teaching model, not Cloudflare's system. Assumptions: one trillion is 1,000 billion and a terabyte is a million megabytes. The 5 billion pairs and 1.6 TB are the figures in Cloudflare's 2025 post. It estimated that about 20% of keys were in use in large data centers and about 1% in small ones. It says all keys together are about 11 times smaller than the whole dataset. The version 1.5 row assumes exactly half of each server's instances hold the full dataset and half hold a cache, although the post says the split became unbalanced. The version 2 row assumes a server that is not a storage server holds only the share of data that is in use. The number of servers, storage servers, lookups and the hit rate are guesses here; the post says the combined hit rate of the first two cache levels was over 99.99% for the worst instance.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, numberValue } from '../../playground';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-est]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const val = numberValue(q);
    const OUT_ROWS = 10; // lines in the result list
    const KEYS_SHARE = 1 / 11; // all keys are about 11 times smaller than the dataset (2025 post)
    const BILLION = 1e9, TB = 1e12, MILLION = 1e6;
    const rows = Array.from({ length: OUT_ROWS }, () => { const dt = document.createElement('dt'); const dd = document.createElement('dd'); q('[data-out]').append(dt, dd); return { dt, dd }; });
    const fmt = (n: number) => (n >= 100 ? Math.round(n) : Math.round(n * 100) / 100).toLocaleString('en-US');
    function draw() {
      const pairs = val('[data-k]') * BILLION; const size = val('[data-s]'); const use = val('[data-u]') / 100;
      const servers = val('[data-n]'); const storage = Math.min(val('[data-w]'), servers); const lookups = val('[data-l]') * MILLION; const hit = val('[data-h]') / 100;
      ['k', 's', 'u', 'n', 'w', 'l'].forEach((k) => (q(`[data-${k}val]`).textContent = String(val(`[data-${k}]`))));
      const cache = size * use;
      const half = size * (0.5 + 0.5 * use);
      const dc = servers * size;
      const dc2 = storage * size + (servers - storage) * cache;
      const reach = lookups * (1 - hit);
      const data: [string, string][] = [
        ['Average size of one pair (bytes)', fmt((size * TB) / pairs)],
        ['One server, version 1: full copy (TB)', fmt(size)],
        ['One server, version 1.5: half full copies, half caches (TB)', fmt(half)],
        ['One server, version 2: cache only (TB)', fmt(cache)],
        ['All keys without values (TB)', fmt(size * KEYS_SHARE)],
        ['Disk saved on a cache-only server (%)', `${fmt(100 * (1 - use))}%`],
        ['Whole data center, every server a full copy (TB)', fmt(dc)],
        ['Whole data center, version 2 (TB)', fmt(dc2)],
        ['Lookups per second that miss every cache and reach storage servers', fmt(reach)],
        [`Per storage server (${storage} of them), lookups per second`, fmt(reach / storage)],
      ];
      rows.forEach((r, i) => { r.dt.textContent = data[i][0]; r.dd.textContent = data[i][1]; });
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
